/*
MDC Rule: PHP Best Practices

- Use strict typing by adding declare(strict_types=1); at the top of every PHP file.
- Follow PSR-12 coding standards for formatting and structure.
- Use namespaces and autoloading for all classes.
- Prefer object-oriented programming (OOP) and SOLID principles.
- Use type hints and return types for all functions and methods.
- Avoid global variables; use dependency injection where possible.
- Write clear, descriptive comments and PHPDoc blocks for all classes, methods, and functions.
- Avoid code duplication by modularizing reusable logic.
- Use Composer for dependency management.
- Write unit and integration tests for all critical code paths.
*/
